From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:22:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Add Teams voice and video calling for the webOS Phone
 app

Add 1:1 Teams calling for personal (Teams for Life) accounts on webOS,
driven by the stock Phone app:

- teams_calling.c/.h: parse the NGC call notifications from the Trouter
  (SDP offer, SRTP key, MS-TURN relay, control links), track call state,
  and answer, reject, hang up and dial over the call control plane. Media
  runs in the separate teams_media helper.
- teams_call_luna.c/.h: the com.palm.teams.call luna-service2 service the
  Phone app's CallSynergizer talks to. It is registered when the plugin
  loads, so it is on the bus before the Phone app subscribes at boot.
- h264_rtp.c/.h, teams_video_relay.cpp/.h, voipkit.cpp/.h: the H.264
  video bridge to legacy webOS's libpalmgstskype.so. voipkit_none.c is a
  null backend for systems without that library, such as LuneOS.
- teams_trouter.c: register the personal calling endpoint
  (SkypeSpacesWeb, TFL context, registrationId = epid, at
  teams.microsoft.com), route /callAgent/ and bare-surl frames to the call
  handler, renew registrations every 5 minutes instead of once a day
  (call routing went stale long before 24 h), and log registrar
  responses.

Calling is only compiled in with -DTEAMS_WEBOS_CALL. Without it the
trouter still prints the "Incoming call" message as upstream does, and
teams_call_log() compiles to nothing. Before this, a build with the
upstream Makefile left teams_calling_handle_trouter and teams_call_log
undefined in the plugin, so libpurple could not load it.

The upstream Makefile does not build these files. A calling build adds
teams_calling.c, teams_call_luna.c, h264_rtp.c, teams_video_relay.cpp and
voipkit.cpp or voipkit_none.c, with -DTEAMS_WEBOS_CALL, the luna-service2
and PmLogLib headers, the directory with webos-ls2-compat.h on the include
path, and links against luna-service2 and libstdc++.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
